    "narrative": "The **Zurich Zebras** lineup is anchored today by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who profiles as our premier start. His matchup against Rhett Lowder is highly favorable, bolstered by a 19% SP skill advantage and a significant 14% platoon boost; most importantly, the presence of an elite base-stealing environment\u2014furthered by a 100% SB opportunity projection\u2014makes him an essential asset in our chase for speed categories. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** (65.92) and **Lars Nootbaar** (64.53) provide high-floor production, with both benefiting from favorable wind conditions blowing out, which should assist their power profiles against Christian Scott and Blade Tidwell, respectively.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (56.85), who narrowly missed the cut for the final UTIL slot. While his 10% park factor adjustment is enticing, the optimizer favored **Carson Benge** (63.22) due to a superior aggregate score derived from a more favorable pitching matchup against Hunter Brown and the added utility of the wind-out factor. We have also opted to keep **Colt Keith** (40.70) on the bench; while he possesses solid raw projection, his negative platoon adjustment against the elite arm of Tarik Skubal makes him a liability today. Managers should exercise caution regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Dillon Dingler** and **Caleb Durbin**, as they face high-tier arms in Skubal and Cam Schlittler; their sub-50 scores leave them on a razor-thin margin, and any negative shift in the batting order could necessitate a pivot to ensure we preserve our remaining game caps.",
